<Group labelreference="L371" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">#Creating the Basis (Now as a function of sm, em, cm, pm). Here, we #suppose some conservations laws to reduce the dimension of fock #space. In fact we use that E + C =E0 +C0 and S + C + P =S 0 + C0 + #P0. In this case, S0=sm, E0=em C0 = P0 =0.  
Baseset:=proc(sm,em,cm,pm) global B; global ket; global bra;global Bdim;
i:=1;

for si from 0 to sm 
    do 
       for ei from 0 to em
           do
              for ci from 0 to cm
                  do 
                     for pri from 0 to pm 
                         do
                         if ei+ci = em then    
                         if si+ci+pri = sm then                            
                         B[i]:=(si,ei,ci,pri); 

                         ket[i]:=Ket(S,si).Ket(E,ei).Ket(C,ci).Ket(P,pri);

                         bra[i]:=Bra(P,pri).Bra(C,ci).Bra(E,ei).Bra(S,si);
                         print(i,B[i] = ket[i]);
                         i:=i+1;
                         end if;
                         end if;
                         end do;
                  end do;
              end do;
        end do;
    Bdim:=i-1;
#for k from 1 to (i-1) do print(i,B[i] = ket[i]); end do;
end proc;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
